ugh the surfaces of living cells and through living membranes generally. <source>Proc. R. Soc. Lond. B. Biol. Sci.</source> <volume>133</volume>:<fpage>140</fpage>&#x02013;200.</citation></ref><ref id="bib19"><citation citation-type="journal">Kuo, A., J.M. Gulbis, J.F. Antcliff, T. Rahman, E.D. Lowe, J. Zimmer, J. Cuthbertson, F.M. Ashcroft, T. Ezaki, and D.A. Doyle. <year>2003</year>. Crystal structure of the potassium channel KirBac1.1 in the closed state. <source>Science.</source> <volume>300</volume>:<fpage>1922</fpage>&#x02013;1926.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12738871</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib20"><citation citation-type="journal">Larsen, E.H. <year>1991</year>. Chloride transport by high resistance heterocellular epithelia. <source>Physiol. Rev.</source> <volume>71</volume>:<fpage>235</fpage>&#x02013;283.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">1986389</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib21"><citation citation-type="journal">Larsen, E.H. <year>2002</year>. Hans H. Ussing&#x02014;scientific work: contemporary significance and perspectives. <source>Biochim. Biophys. Acta.</source> <volume>1566</volume>:<fpage>2</fpage>&#x02013;15.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12421533</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib22"><citation citation-type="journal">Marmont, G. <year>1949</year>. Studies on the axon membrane; a new method. <source>J. Cell. Physiol.</source> <volume>34</volume>:<fpage>351</fpage>&#x02013;382.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15406358</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib23"><citation citation-type="journal">Morth, J.P., B.P. Pedersen, M.S. Toustrup-Jensen, T.L. Sorensen, J. Petersen, J.P. Andersen, B. Vilsen, and P. Nissen. <year>2007</year>. Crystal structure of the sodium-potassium pump. <source>Nature.</source> <volume>450</volume>:<fpage>1043</fpage>&#x02013;1049.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">18075585</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib24"><citation citation-type="journal">Murer, H., U. Hopfer, and R. Kinne. <year>1976</year>. Sodium/proton antiport in brush-border-membrane vesicles from rat small intestine and kidney. <source>Biochem. J.</source> <volume>154</volume>:<fpage>597</fpage>&#x02013;604.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">942389</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib25"><citation citation-type="journal">O'Neil, R.G., and E.L. Boulpaep. <year>1982</year>. Ionic conductive properties and electrophysiology of the rabbit cortical collecting tubule. <source>Am. J. Physiol.</source> <volume>243</volume>:<fpage>F81</fpage>&#x02013;F95.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7091368</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib26"><citation citation-type="other">Reuss, L. <year>2008</year>. Mechanisms of ion transport across cell membranes and epithelia. <italic>In</italic> The Kindey: Physiology and Pathophysiology, 4th Edition. R.J. Alpern and S.C. Hebert, editors. Academic Press, Burlington, MA. 35&#x02013;56.</citation></ref><ref id="bib27"><citation citation-type="journal">Riklis, E., and J.H. Quastel. <year>1958</year>. Effects of cations on sugar absorption by isolated surviving guinea pig intestine. <source>Can. J. Biochem. Physiol.</source> <volume>36</volume>:<fpage>347</fpage>&#x02013;362.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">13511241</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib28"><citation citation-type="journal">Rodriguez-Boulan, E., G. Kreitzer, and A. M&#x000fc;sch. <year>2005</year>. Organization of vesicular trafficking in epithelia. <source>Nat. Rev. Mol. Cell Biol.</source> <volume>6</volume>:<fpage>233</fpage>&#x02013;247.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15738988</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib29"><citation citation-type="journal">Schultz, S.G., and R. Zalusky. <year>1964</year>. Ion transport in isolated rabbit ileum II. Interaction between active sodium and active sugar transport. <source>J. Gen. Physiol.</source> <volume>47</volume>:<fpage>1043</fpage>&#x02013;1059.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">14192544</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib30"><citation citation-type="journal">Sharp, G.W.G., and A. Leaf. <year>1966</year>. Mechanism of action of al